  "statement": "An alchemist produces synthetic gold crystals in N stages. At stage i (from 1 to N), the reaction energy is (A^i) mod M.\n\nGiven integers A, N, and M, calculate the sum of energies produced across all N stages:\nTotal Energy = ( sum_{i=1}^N (A^i mod M) ) mod M.",
  "inputFormat": "Three space-separated integers A, N, and M.",
  "outputFormat": "Print the total energy modulo M.",
  "constraints": "1 <= A <= 10^9, 1 <= N <= 10^6, 1 <= M <= 10^9",
  "sampleCases": [
    {
      "input": "2 3 5",
      "expectedOutput": "4",
      "explanation": "i=1: 2^1%5=2; i=2: 2^2%5=4; i=3: 2^3%5=3. Sum = 2+4+3 = 9. 9%5 = 4."
    },
    {
      "input": "3 4 7",
      "expectedOutput": "1",
      "explanation": "3^1%7=3, 3^2%7=2, 3^3%7=6, 3^4%7=4. Sum = 15. 15%7 = 1."
    }
  ],
